  "raw": " Tito broke free of Ustaše influence for the rest of his life. One year after his Revolutionary experience in Berlin, the second world war began when Germany declared war on Finland. Despite this conflict, which led to thousands killed and many more displaced or destitute refugees, brothers resumed their wrestling after winning a few medals under the Soviet flag as table-tennis champions. Strongest was Marijan, but he later collapsed from a stroke at the age of 30. Meanwhile two girls came up based on both strength and personality: Bohdan died in an accidental boating accident while lying to him about political connections, leaving Ona . Their strong personalities built mutual arguments into daily habits. This game was played until 1941, still one of the most popular subjects among young men.\nFrom 1936, the Yugoslav feels attracted by Castro's Cuba , Brazil, India, Chinese Jimmie Gang, Vietnam Revolution with Vietnamese unification . insistence that \"Decolonization is not only a medical problem \". Under Tit",
  "serialized": "Tito broke free of Ustaše influence for the rest of his life. One year after his Revolutionary experience in Berlin, the second world war began when Germany declared war on Finland. Despite this conflict, which led to thousands killed and many more displaced or destitute refugees, brothers resumed their wrestling after winning a few medals under the Soviet flag as table-tennis champions. Strongest was Marijan, but he later collapsed from a stroke at the age of 30. Meanwhile two girls came up based on both strength and personality: Bohdan died in an accidental boating accident while lying to him about political connections, leaving Ona . Their strong personalities built mutual arguments into daily habits. This game was played until 1941, still one of the most popular subjects among young men. From 1936, the Yugoslav feels attracted by Castro's Cuba , Brazil, India, Chinese Jimmie Gang, Vietnam Revolution with Vietnamese unification . insistence that \"Decolonization is not only a medical problem \". Under Tit",
